/-!
# Buckholtz polynomials and rational coefficients for exponential partial sums

In Buckholtz's uniform asymptotic expansion of the scaled exponential partial sums
`∑_{k ≤ n} (n z)^k / k!` away from `z = 1` (DLMF 8.11.18–8.11.19), the coefficient sequence `d_k`
is generated by `d_0(z) = z / (1 - z)` and `d_{k+1}(z) = -(z / (1 - z)) d_k'(z)`. Writing
`d_k(z) = (-1)^k z p_k(z) / (1 - z)^{2k + 1}` exhibits integer numerator polynomials
`p_k ∈ ℤ[X]` (`TauCeti.expPartialSumPoly`) with nonnegative coefficients satisfying `p_0 = 1` and
`p_{k+1}(X) = (1 + 2k X) p_k(X) + X (1 - X) p_k'(X)`, whose reflection `p_k(-X)` is the polynomial
sequence `A_k` governing the large-order uniform expansion of the generalized exponential integral
`E_p(λ p)` (DLMF 8.20.4–8.20.6).

This module defines `TauCeti.expPartialSumPoly` and `TauCeti.expPartialSumCoeff` and establishes
their degree, positivity, differential recurrence, uniqueness, ordered-field monotonicity, and
uniform norm bounds on complex wedges and real half-lines. See
`TauCeti.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Exp.PartialSums.Basic` for the resulting uniform asymptotic
expansions.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.expPartialSumPoly`: the numerator polynomial sequence `p_k ∈ ℤ[X]` satisfying
  `p_0 = 1` and `p_{k+1}(X) = (1 + 2k X) p_k(X) + X (1 - X) p_k'(X)`.
* `TauCeti.expPartialSumCoeff`: the rational coefficient sequence
  `d_k(z) = (-1)^k z p_k(z) / (1 - z)^{2k + 1}` of DLMF 8.11.18–8.11.19 over any field.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.eval_one_expPartialSumPoly`, `TauCeti.natDegree_expPartialSumPoly`,
  `TauCeti.leadingCoeff_expPartialSumPoly`, `TauCeti.one_le_aeval_expPartialSumPoly`,
  `TauCeti.comp_neg_X_expPartialSumPoly_succ`: degree `k - 1`, leading coefficient `k!`, value
  `(2k - 1)‼` at `1`, positivity on `[0, ∞)`, and the DLMF 8.20.4 recurrence for `p_k(-X)`.
* `TauCeti.expPartialSumCoeff_def`, `TauCeti.hasDerivAt_expPartialSumCoeff`,
  `TauCeti.expPartialSumCoeff_succ_eq_neg_div_mul_deriv`,
  `TauCeti.eq_expPartialSumCoeff_of_recurrence`: defining rational formula, the differential
  recurrence `d_{k+1}(z) = -(z / (1 - z)) d_k'(z)` of DLMF 8.11.19, and its uniqueness off `z = 1`.
* `TauCeti.neg_one_pow_mul_expPartialSumCoeff_nonneg`,
  `TauCeti.neg_one_pow_mul_expPartialSumCoeff_pos`,
  `TauCeti.neg_one_pow_mul_expPartialSumCoeff_mono`: positivity and monotonicity of `(-1)^k d_k` on
  `[0, 1)` over any linearly ordered field.
* `TauCeti.norm_expPartialSumCoeff_le_of_re_le`, `TauCeti.abs_expPartialSumCoeff_le`: uniform
  explicit bounds on complex wedges and on `(-∞, 1 - δ]`.

## References

* *NIST Digital Library of Mathematical Functions*, [§8.11(v)](https://dlmf.nist.gov/8.11#v),
  Eqs. 8.11.18 and 8.11.19, and [§8.20(ii)](https://dlmf.nist.gov/8.20#ii), Eqs. 8.20.4–8.20.5.
* J. D. Buckholtz, *Concerning an approximation of Copson*, Proc. Amer. Math. Soc. **14** (1963),
  564–568.
* F. G. Tricomi, *Asymptotische Eigenschaften der unvollständigen Gammafunktion*, Math. Z. **53**
  (1950), 136–148.
* N. M. Temme, *Special Functions: An Introduction to the Classical Functions of Mathematical
  Physics*, Wiley, 1996, §11.2.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open Polynomial
